      "text": "To determine the probability that both selected members are girls from a club of 10 members (5 boys and 5 girls), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10.**\n\n   The number of ways to choose 2 members from 10 is given by the combination formula:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5.**\n\n   The number of ways to choose 2 girls from 5 is given by the combination formula:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the probability that both selected members are girls.**\n\n   The probability is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes (choosing 2 girls) to the total number of outcomes (choosing any 2 members):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of ways to choose 2 girls}}{\\text{Number of ways to choose 2 members}} = \\frac{10}{45} = \\frac{2}{9}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that both selected members are girls is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\\).",
